    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>Neil Sutton is an Australian businessman from the family behind Sydney's Suttons Motors. He inherited a share of the dealership business from his father, Sir Frederick Sutton, and later sold it. He directed the proceeds into a family trust, building a portfolio of property and business investments beyond the original car trade.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "At Suttons Motors, Neil Sutton taught salesman Michael Pallier to make full use of the time a customer spent at the dealership. While a trade-in was being valued, staff could review its service history and discuss the next purchase. He also stressed asking for the order before the customer left to visit a rival dealer.\n\nWith his son, Scott, Sutton bought Gladesville Bridge Marina through their company SNJ. They also owned the Boutique Boat Company at Rose Bay. The marina business proposed replacing some swing moorings with floating berths and adding capacity for larger craft.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 89,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Pallier gives a detailed first-person account of Sutton as his boss and sales teacher. Separate reporting establishes the father-son commercial ownership and the proposed marina changes."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S5",
      "S6"
    ],
    "word_count": 95,
    "html": "<p>At Suttons Motors, Neil Sutton taught salesman Michael Pallier to make full use of the time a customer spent at the dealership. While a trade-in was being valued, staff could review its service history and discuss the next purchase. He also stressed asking for the order before the customer left to visit a rival dealer.</p>\r\n<p>With his son, Scott, Sutton bought Gladesville Bridge Marina through their company SNJ. They also owned the Boutique Boat Company at Rose Bay. The marina business proposed replacing some swing moorings with floating berths and adding capacity for larger craft.</p>\r\n"
  },
